Atlas overlay patch 0123: fed/fed-guard
Why: a Federate name is exclusively fed:// (lead rule 2026-11-05, ADR 0052), so no code path of the browser may
 look one up in DNS or open a socket to it. Two fences besides the loaders of patch 0121. (1) The DNS prefetch and
 preconnect predictors (loading predictor, network hints from <link rel=dns-prefetch|preconnect>, omnibox) all
 use one content::PreconnectManager; the loading predictor's is wrapped by FedPreconnectGuard, which drops every
 call about a host under a Federate TLD before the real manager sees it. (2) The browser adds one host-resolver
 rule per Federate TLD (MAP *.fed ~NOTFOUND, ...) to its own --host-resolver-rules at startup, which content
 passes on to the network service: whatever path is left (a redirect from the web, WebSocket, prefetch, an
 extension) cannot resolve such a name. The rules go in before the network service starts.
Files: chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc, chrome/browser/predictors/loading_predictor.cc, chrome/browser/predictors/BUILD.gn
Test filter: *AtlasFedExclusive*; journey: a page with <link rel=dns-prefetch href=//home.fed> makes no lookup, ws://x.fed fails to resolve
Rebase risk: L (a one-line call at the top of a constructor, one include, one wrapped call, one dependency)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, base tree plus the patches before it in the series (dev slot 4)

